A||N||7||SKIDMARK||3.4 uprade||||3||
Z||000000||SKIDMARK||10-12-2001||02:00 PM||||I think I made the decision to upgrade to the 3.4. Just a couple of questions that I didn't see clearly answered in past threads.<P>1. What upgrades if any are needed to the fuel injection and ecm? I've heard anywhere from just an adjustable regulator to replace the injectors with 3.4 style and an HO pump.<BR>2. Is ther a template or blueprint or sketch on a napkin that gives details of drilling/machining to relocate the starter? <BR>3. If I get a short block, will my iron heads, 2.8 oilpan and harmonic balancer work with the 3.4? I know I will need a new flexplate.<BR>Any other problem areas that I should be aware of please let me know.<P>Thanks in advance,<P>              Don<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000001||187bk||10-12-2001||02:30 PM||||On the note of drilling for a starter, that shouldn't be nessacery unless you have a RWD motor. If you did, you'd have to get an oil filter relocation kit, and you would then just drill the new holes for the starter opposite of where they are now.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||10-12-2001||02:44 PM||||In order to install a 3.4 and retain the looks of the 2.8 you need touse the 3.4 RWD motor from the Camaro.<P>As for redrilling the starter..I believe there is a template floating around that can be rented.<P>There is a Chip out there for the conversion made by Joe Wyman (sp?) I have also heard of people using a chip for a tpi 305 iroc with a lot of success.<P>I have heard of people using stock injectors, pump and ecm. Obviously the motor doesn't run to it's full potential. There are numerous injectors that are plug and play and are readily available. Mustang 19lbs injectors , 305 , 350 TPI injecotrs , 3.1 injectors. All plug and play. You can also swap in a 89 Turbo trans am pump , or a TPI fuel pump . Both I beileve are in the $65 range. <P>Depends on what you want. A basic swap , or are you building up the motor to be more performance minded?<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||10-12-2001||03:28 PM||||I did a 3.4 in my car. Talking from experience here. I don't know where that  info on relocating the oil filter is coming from but is not true. Someone here has the template for drilling . Regarding the fuel system, there is nothing that you need to add for a stock setup. I'm using 2.8 injectors and stock fuel pump and I haven't been able to lean it. I do have a Hypertech chip which I bought 10 years ago for a 2.8. Also I have a FPR which is now at stock 43psi with no problem. Heads and balancer will work. Not sure on oil pan for pre 88. I used stock one in my 88 Formula. Read a lot about this topic before jumping on and getting unnecessary expensive parts.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:||||reg||1
Z||000004||SKIDMARK||10-13-2001||10:21 PM||||bump<BR>I really could use info on relocating the starter.||||reg||1
Z||000005||danny boy||10-14-2001||12:58 AM||||Black88GT had the template I think. Worked great. When we did the swap in Formulas car we used a timing cover and oilpan from an 86 engine I had. Without that template, it'd be really hard.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula||10-14-2001||01:59 AM||||and put a little bit of oil on the bit!<P>they might not be too expensive but breaking them really slows things down!||||reg||1
Z||000007||BC-GT||10-14-2001||02:21 AM||||Best pics I've seen are here(for the starter relocation) As for the template mentioned earlier, I have it for sale in the mall section now, never got to use it though.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/eswap/eswap.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/eswap/eswap.html</A> <BR>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by BC-GT (edited 10-14-2001).]||||reg||1
